  "comment": "Intel Atom is the brand name for a line of ultra-low-voltage x86 and x86-64 CPUs (or microprocessors ) from Intel , designed in 45 nm CMOS and used mainly in netbooks , nettops , and Mobile Internet devices (MIDs). On December 21, 2009 Intel announced the next generation of Atom processors, including the N450, with total kit power consumption down 40%. Contents 1 History 2 Availability 3",
